apps/lotus-explore-rs/public/assets/ketcher/
apps/lotus-explore-rs/public/assets/vendor/

# The fetcher vendors into the crate it runs from as well as the app. Neither
# tree is source: it is fetched by `cargo run -p lotus-web-assets --bin
# fetch-assets` and is reproducible from the versions in that binary.
crates/lotus-web-assets/public/

# The same tree, at the workspace root, which is where `fetch-assets` writes if it
# is run from there rather than from the app crate. The Dockerfile comment says why
# that matters -- a root-level `public/` is one nothing reads, so the build then
# succeeds with no assets in it -- which is a bad enough failure that it is worth
# being unable to commit by accident rather than merely unlikely to.
/public/assets/
/public/

# Project-specific agent tooling not covered by global gitignore
.code-review-graph/
GEMINI.md
*.agent-scratch*
.ignore
